From 842c6dc2e73969814083372d89c7f35bce109dce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:55:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 19/31] Gui: translate enumeration values in the property
 editor; Japanese property texts

- Enumeration values were shown as the raw strings of the property
  ("One side", "Length"). Show them translated (context
  App::PropertyEnumeration, separate from property names since the same
  word can mean different things, e.g. "Normal"), while the editor keeps
  and sets the property's own values.
- Japanese translations for the names, groups and tooltips of the
  properties of the Part, PartDesign, Sketcher, Measure, TechDraw, Mesh
  and Spreadsheet objects and their view providers (about 1170 texts,
  collected from the objects themselves), and for 238 enumeration values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
